{%- doc -%}
  RB-001 — the crystal player shell (Stage 3: live content).

  ARCHITECTURE (locked): the Blender render is the complete physical
  interface — crystal, glass housings, capsule, optical edges. This
  snippet renders that ONE image plus an overlay of empty, transparent
  hooks. Shopify owns every piece of content; Blender owns every piece
  of glass. Nothing product-specific may be written into this file.

  Stage 3: assets/rb001-ui.js (loaded from snippets/scripts.liquid)
  populates every hook from the ArchiveOS bus exactly as
  archive-ui.js populates the transport deck. This file still renders
  no product data itself — the record travels over the bus, and the
  data contract lives in the rb001-ui.js header.

  COORDINATES: every zone is positioned by the Frame-B calibration map
  in assets/rb001-player.css — shell-relative percentages measured
  through the locked Blender camera (see the Stage-1 audit). Do not
  add positioning here, and do not invent percentages there.

  The buttons carry no chrome. The rendered glass IS the button.
  Stage 3B adds the GLYPHS as content: inline SVG reproductions of the
  measured Blender glyph objects (PI6_Play / PI6_Next / PI6_Previous /
  PI6_HeartGlyph), sized and centred by their measured glyph-to-housing
  ratios. They draw no circles, borders or backgrounds of their own.
{%- enddoc -%}

{{ 'rb001-player.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="rb001" data-rb001 data-rb001-stage="3d">
  <img
    class="rb001__shell"
    src="{{ 'rb001-shell-collapsed.png' | asset_url }}"
    alt=""
    width="1743"
    height="690"
    decoding="async"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >

  {%- comment -%} ---- content zones (empty hooks, Stage 3 fills them) ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rb001__zone rb001__zone--artwork" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- comment -%}
      No src attribute at all until a track is seated. An empty src=""
      resolves against the page URL, so the browser really does issue a
      request for the document as an image and logs a failure on every
      idle shell. The Stage-3B artwork zone starts genuinely empty.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <img class="rb001__artwork is-showing" data-rb001-artwork-a alt="">
    <img class="rb001__artwork" data-rb001-artwork-b alt="">
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    IDENTITY. Stage 3B: each line is its own box at the coordinates of
    the matching Blender text object, measured through the locked camera
    (see the calibration table in assets/rb001-player.css). The wrapper
    is a bare positioning context, not a panel.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rb001__zone rb001__zone--identity">
    {%- comment -%} Static UI label — not track data. {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="rb001__line rb001__nowplaying" aria-hidden="true">NOW PLAYING</p>
    <h2 class="rb001__line rb001__title" data-rb001-title></h2>
    <p class="rb001__line rb001__producer" data-rb001-producer></p>
    <p class="rb001__line rb001__meta">
      <span data-rb001-bpm></span>
      <span data-rb001-key></span>
      <span data-rb001-tags></span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <span class="rb001__zone rb001__zone--time" data-rb001-time></span>

  <div class="rb001__zone rb001__zone--waveform">
    <div class="rb001__waveform" data-rb001-waveform aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ---- transparent hit areas over the rendered glass ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Glyphs, and where each one's authority comes from:

      play   Single triangle, 3 verts (0,1)(1,0.5)(0,0). The SHAPE is
             Blender's PI6_Play; the box it fills is the reference's,
             which is wider and shorter (Stage 3D).
      heart  Purpose-built stroked outline (Stage 3D). Bfont's U+2661
             contour carried a hairline — 3.5% of the glyph width — where
             the reference draws a heavy 15% stroke, and a font contour
             cannot be re-weighted. This is a centreline path stroked to
             the measured weight; its envelope and optical drop are still
             PI6_HeartGlyph's.
      prev
      next   The CANONICAL REFERENCE, not Blender (Stage 3C). Blender's
             prev/next are single triangles, but PI6_Previous is a stale
             object — permanently hidden, and sunk 0.72 units below the
             glass the other glyphs share — and the reference draws the
             pair as double chevrons. Each mark is two identical
             triangles: the second begins at 0.463 of the box and each
             spans 0.537, so they abut with a 0.074 overlap. Those two
             figures are the step and span measured off the reference's
             own ink-per-column profile, and prev is the exact mirror.

    Every size and offset is a ratio of the housing box, so the glyphs
    scale with the shell and need no viewport rules.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--prev" data-rb001-prev aria-label="Previous artifact" disabled><svg class="rb001__glyph" viewBox="0 0 1 1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M1 0L.463 .5L1 1Z"/><path d="M.537 0L0 .5L.537 1Z"/></svg></button>
  <button type="button" class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--play" data-rb001-play aria-label="Play" disabled><svg class="rb001__glyph" viewBox="0 0 1 1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M0 0L1 .5L0 1Z"/></svg></button>
  <button type="button" class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--next" data-rb001-next aria-label="Next artifact" disabled><svg class="rb001__glyph" viewBox="0 0 1 1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M0 0L.537 .5L0 1Z"/><path d="M.463 0L1 .5L.463 1Z"/></svg></button>
  {%- comment -%}
    Favorite is VISUAL ONLY in Stage 3B. There is no favorites mechanism
    anywhere in the theme, so the control stays disabled rather than
    growing a private one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--heart" data-rb001-heart aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Favorite" disabled><svg class="rb001__glyph rb001__glyph--stroked" viewBox="-8.82 -8.82 117.65 110.60" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M50 25C50 11.19 61.19 0 75 0C88.81 0 100 11.19 100 25C100 52 62 72 50 92.95C38 72 0 52 0 25C0 11.19 11.19 0 25 0C38.81 0 50 11.19 50 25Z"/></svg></button>
  {%- comment -%}
    ACQUIRE LICENSE (Stage 2). Real Shopify text over the rendered
    glass pill — the glass is the chrome, this element is only text,
    interaction and accessibility. Label comes from the locale, never
    hard-coded. Destination: Stage-2 safe fallback is the product URL
    when Liquid has product context (the current deck mount); Stage 3
    upgrades data-rb001-acquire to the licence-region scroll/queue
    behaviour via the ArchiveOS bus. Without product context it stays
    a disabled control rather than a dead link.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product -%}
    <a class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--acquire" data-rb001-acquire href="{{ product.url }}">
      <span class="rb001__acquire-label">{{ 'actions.acquire_license' | t }}</span>
    </a>
  {%- else -%}
    <button type="button" class="rb001__hit rb001__hit--acquire" data-rb001-acquire disabled>
      <span class="rb001__acquire-label">{{ 'actions.acquire_license' | t }}</span>
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
